          "field_group": "NARRATIVE",
          "field_path": "narrative",
          "value": "A 58-year-old female patient with a history of hypertension and type 2 diabetes began Velmoradine 20 mg once daily on 3 March 2026. Nine days later, on 12 March 2026, she developed a widespread itchy maculopapular rash across the trunk and both forearms. The drug was withdrawn on 13 March and the rash began to settle within 48 hours. No corticosteroid was required. She had taken no other new medicine in the preceding month.",
